<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tehran</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tehran is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, lying at the southern foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alborz">Alborz</a> mountains. Once a village near the ancient city of Rey, it grew under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavids</a> and was made the capital by Agha Mohammad Khan, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar dynasty</a>, in 1786. It remained the seat of government under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-persian">Pahlavis</a> and the Islamic Republic and is one of the largest cities in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tehran.jpg" alt="Tehran" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ninara from Helsinki, Finland · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:North_of_Tehran_Skyline_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
